note: every form of an interface
something that can speak is anything with:
    a way to speak.
    a way to greet with name (text) and count (a number), giving back text.
    a way to answer, giving back yes or no.
a speaker is anything with:
    a way to speak.
let pets be an empty list of things that can speak.
let loud be an empty list of speakers.
to introduce with pet (something that can speak or nothing):
    speak pet.
say greet pet with "Ann" and 2.
